    <p>Levels 11–31 and 33+ are being verified the same way — one level at a time, no shortcuts. More wave maps coming shortly.</p>
    <InContentAd />

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is Rotate Rings?</summary><p>Rotate Rings is a free-to-play rotation puzzle by Nebula Studio for iOS and Android. The board is a network of colored pipe segments — C-shapes, L-shapes, straight pieces and closed circles joined by silver connectors. You spin the loose segments until each color closes a complete loop; every closed loop bursts off the board, and bursts can chain-reaction into neighboring loops.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How many levels does Rotate Rings have?</summary><p>Full-game walkthrough videos cover levels 1 to 200, and community trackers list up to 260 levels. The game updates weekly, so new levels keep arriving — we add walkthroughs as we verify them.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is Rotate Rings free?</summary><p>Yes — Rotate Rings is free to download and play on iOS and Android. After each cleared level you land on the Acorn Challenge screen, a leaderboard mini-game built around the acorns you collected during the level.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How are these walkthroughs verified?</summary><p>Every walkthrough is checked against real gameplay footage frame by frame: burst timestamps, piece colors, scores and the endgame sequence are all read off the video before anything is written. Waves timed at 4 frames per second carry a full-verification badge; waves timed at 1 frame per second carry a star badge and a ±1 second tolerance. Nothing is published that we could not confirm on screen.</p></details>

